Formulas: a Latex is std's record {latex: String}, made by `latex` from LaTeX source, usually a template, whose
backslashes are text. `latexSource` reads it back, and `latexEscape` makes text safe to typeset literally.
$[Import* std]
${latex f"{\frac{1}{2} + \nabla}"}
expect: {latex: "\\frac{1}{2} + \\nabla"}
$[# a {latex "x^2"}]
${latex f"{\sqrt{${latexSource a} + ${+ 1 2}}}"}
expect: {latex: "\\sqrt{x^2 + 3}"}
$[# label "a_b {c} 50% \\ ^ ~"]
${latexEscape label}
expect: "a\\_b \\{c\\} 50\\% \\text{\\textbackslash} \\text{\\textasciicircum} \\text{\\textasciitilde}"
${latexSource {latex f"{$$\alpha}"}}
expect: "$\\alpha"
${= {latex "x"} {latex "x"}} ${.latex {: {latex "x"} Latex}}
expect: true
expect: "x"
${latexSource {latex f"{
    \begin{aligned}
      y &= ${latexSource a}
    \end{aligned}
    }"}}
expect: "\\begin{aligned}\n  y &= x^2\n\\end{aligned}\n"
